4,85,86,80],"stages","Planning","Gameplay & code","Testing","Topics",[90,91,92,93,94],"tags","code-world-model","simulation-generation","POMDP","benchmark","NeurIPS-2024","Further reading",[97,98],{"_52":101,"_25":58},{"_52":99,"_25":100},"Paper v2 scope","https://arxiv.org/html/2409.17652v2","Project","Project source",[104],{"_52":102,"_25":105},"https://arxiv.org/abs/2409.17652","Why it belongs here","Generative Simulation via Factorized Representation uses a factorized POMDP representation to reduce context per generation step. It generates 2D game simulations for agent training. Its robotics experiments generate task code, including object states and reward structure, within the existing CLIPort framework. The game benchmark covers eight Pygame environments; 3D game generation is future work in the NeurIPS 2024 paper. Robotics experiments retain 3D relevance without establishing generation of a complete physics engine.","detail","guidance","Resource type","Paper","Category","category","lead","summary","name","world","paper",[129,130],[90,91,92,93,94],[126,127,128,117],[124,125,117],2024,"2d","3d","plan","code","test",{"_52":101,"_25":58},{"_52":99,"_25":100},{"_132":133},"documents",{"_134":135,"_136":137},"en",[139,143,144,145,142,146,147,148,149,150,151,152,153,154,155,156,157,158,159,160,161,162,163,164,165,166,167,168,169,170,171,172,173,174,175,176,177,141,178,140,179,180,181,182,183,184,185,186,187,188,189,190,191,192,193,194,195,196,197,198,199],"zh",[138,139,140,141,142],"reading-guide","practical-guide","level-design-skill","deployment","publishing-platforms","tutorials-and-demos","coding-agent-game-code","game-testing-library","agents-notes","engines-notes","game-ai-notes","cadle-repositories","world-model-notes","research-index","production-research-notes","engine-operation-contracts","production-work-orders","studio-production-case-studies","native-operation-details","production-debugging-contracts","production-coverage-gaps","generative-tools-resear